SUMMARY:maptimeDavis: Intro to QGIS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T120000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54038458841458
DESCRIPTION:This introductory-level workshop will focus upon the fundament
 al concepts and skills needed to explore and analyze data using Geographic
  Information Systems (GIS) software with examples using the QGIS platform.
 \n \n\nSpeaker: Holden Tal\n \n\nHolden is a Master Student in the Geograp
 hy Graduate Group who is studying the hazards of small coastal communities
 .\n \n\nPrerequisites: None\n \n\nSoftware Required: Please download and i
 nstall QGIS (version 3.44.7 Solothurn) from qgis.org
LOCATION:DataLab Classroom\, 360 Shields Library
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/maptimedavis-intro-to-qgis
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UC Davis Library": "https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-publish-your-first-scientific-paper"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_library
SUMMARY:Workshop: So you’re ready to publish your first scientific paper
 ?...
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53949248324551
DESCRIPTION:Publishing research in a scientific journal is a critical step
  in every researcher's journey. However\, it can be a very complex and int
 imidating landscape when doing it for the first time. This workshop will p
 rovide an introduction to major parts of the process including\, an overvi
 ew of the scientific publishing landscape\, selecting a journal\, working 
 with collaborators\, and more! This workshop is aimed at all STEM-aligned 
 fields and all experience levels\, but beginners are especially welcome.\n
 \n \n\nRegister:\n\nZoom Registration\n\nIn-Person Registration
LOCATION:Walker Hall\, Gibeling Room or Zoom
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-publish-your-first-s
 cientific-paper
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
